{
 "comment": "clause44: a line is placed by its own ledger before the voucher's party is read: the depreciation set, then a judgement money category, then the no-supplier list, then a forced category (bank interest to the exempt column, bank charges to 'other than composition'), whatever the party: a journal with no party, a party that is itself an expense ledger, a party that is an income ledger, a party named on no ledger master, a registered supplier with no tax line, an unregistered one. A forced category on a depreciation ledger or on a no-supplier ledger keeps the reason; a judgement category keeps its reason; a ledger with no category is still read by the party ('no party' on a journal with none, whose forced sibling on the same voucher is in its column), and interest to an individual lender is read by the party and counted as a judgement candidate. Every GSTIN is invented (fourteenth character Y).",
